---
description: Require a tested dev build before production EAS builds when native changes exist
alwaysApply: true
---

# Dev build before production

Before running any `eas build --profile production` command, check whether the changes since the last production build include any of the following:

- New or updated native modules / packages (anything requiring native linking)
- New or changed Expo config plugins in `app.json`
- New or changed permissions (notifications, camera, location, etc.)
- Any change to native config (`Info.plist`, entitlements, `AndroidManifest`, etc.)

If any of the above apply and a **dev build has not yet been built and tested on-device** with these specific changes, **STOP** and tell the user:

> These changes touch native code/plugins. Recommend running a dev build first (`eas build --profile development`) and testing on-device before a production build.

Do **not** proceed to a production build until the user confirms a dev build was tested, or confirms the changes are pure JS/TS with no native impact.

Apply this same check before suggesting or running any `eas submit` command.
